---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SOCIAL } from "@/config/site-config";

const effectiveDate = { iso: "2026-10-22", label: "October 22, 2026" };
---

<Layout
	title="SPS Terms of Service"
	ogImage="images/social-preview.png"
	description="Terms for using the Self Prompting System (SPS), a private Discord application.">
	<article>
		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">cat ~/sps/TERMS</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-file-earmark-text"></i> SPS Terms of Service</h2>
			<p>
				These terms cover use of the <b>Self Prompting System</b> ("SPS") Discord application, a private, experimental tool
				I operate. They don't cover this website; for that, see <a href="/notes/2026-03-12-licensing/"
					>Licensing &amp; Disclaimer</a
				>.
			</p>
			<p>
				Effective <time datetime={effectiveDate.iso}>{effectiveDate.label}</time>. Read them alongside the <a
					href="/sps/privacy/">SPS Privacy Policy</a
				>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps --about</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-terminal"></i> What SPS is</h2>
			<p>
				SPS is a Windows-first orchestration system that runs locally and carries out engineering work through Claude
				Code and Codex CLI workflows. Its Discord interface is intended to let authorized operators see progress, give
				feedback, control authorized runs, and record explicit decisions, using slash commands, buttons, and forms.
			</p>
			<p>
				A supervised fixture controller exists today. <b>The Discord interface is planned and not yet operational.</b>
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps auth --scope</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-person-check"></i> Who may use it</h2>
			<p>
				Only people I have explicitly authorized. Authorization covers the projects and scope I have approved, and
				nothing beyond them. Please don't use SPS outside that scope or try to get around the limits on who can use it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps verify --trust-nothing</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-robot"></i> AI-generated output</h2>
			<p>
				Work produced through SPS, and the status summaries it reports, may be generated by AI tools. They can be
				incomplete or wrong. Verify anything that matters before relying on it; operator review is still required.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps approve --physical</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-exclamation-triangle"></i> Approvals don't replace physical steps</h2>
			<p>
				Approving something in Discord does not satisfy a step that requires a physical action or an in-person
				observation. Those steps still have to be carried out and observed directly.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">sps uptime</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-hourglass-split"></i> Access and availability</h2>
			<p>
				I may suspend or revoke access for misuse, security concerns, or operational reasons. SPS is experimental, and I
				don't guarantee that it will be available or run without interruption.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">ls ~/sps/third-party/</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-link-45deg"></i> Other terms that apply</h2>
			<p>Using SPS through Discord also means Discord's terms apply, as do the terms of the model providers involved:</p
			>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<a href="https://discord.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord Terms of Service</a>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a
						href="https://support-dev.discord.com/hc/en-us/articles/8563934450327-Discord-Developer-Policy"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord Developer Policy</a
					>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/consumer-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>Anthropic Consumer Terms of Service</a
					>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a href="https://openai.com/policies/terms-of-use/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>OpenAI Terms of Use</a
					>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-10">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-success font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">git log -- ~/sps/TERMS</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<h2><i class="icon-calendar-event"></i> Changes and contact</h2>
			<p>
				Material changes will be reflected on this page with an updated date. Once the Discord interface is active,
				authorized operators will also get a notice when these terms change.
			</p>
			<p>
				Questions go to <a href={`mailto:${SOCIAL.email}`}>{SOCIAL.email}</a>. Last updated <time
					datetime={effectiveDate.iso}>{effectiveDate.label}</time
				>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<hr class="my-8 border-base-300" />

		<section class="mb-6">
			<p class="text-xs text-neutral-content mb-2">
				<span class="text-error font-bold">$</span>
				<span class="ml-1 text-warning">exit</span>
				<span class="blink" aria-hidden="true">_</span>
			</p>
			<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-4">
				<a href="/sps/privacy/" class="link-action no-underline">
					<i class="icon-shield-check"></i>
					SPS Privacy
				</a>
				<a href="/notes/2026-03-12-licensing/" class="link-action no-underline">
					<i class="icon-info-circle"></i>
					Licensing
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>
</Layout>
